# Changelog

All notable changes are documented here, newest first. See also the [releases page](https://github.com/results-may-vary-org/tape/releases).

## v4.0.2 (2026-08-30) 🎨

The overall release — a complete visual rework of the app.

- New themes: 11 built-in themes, including Catppuccin, Rosé Pine, Tokyo Night and more
- Vim motions in the editor (toggle from settings or `Ctrl+W`)
- Line numbers: none, relative or normal
- Optional last-edited timestamp under each file name in the file tree
- Fully responsive UI/UX, redesigned from the ground up (works even below 300px)
- Links in the reader now open in your default browser
- Live config editing from the settings menu, with validation and linting for every key
- Unsaved changes protection: you are warned before switching notes or closing the app
- AUR package is up to date

## v3.7.3 (2025-05-05) ✨

Quick fix release.

- Fix the version tag shown in the app so it displays the current version correctly
- Fix the GitHub action workflow to build for webkit 4.0 and 4.1
- AUR is up to date

## v3.7.1 (2025-04-08)

Quick fix release for webkit2gtk.

- Linux fix for a problem with `webkit2gtk`; Linux users should use this version instead of v3.7.0
- For other platforms, see v3.7.0

## v3.7.0 (2025-03-29) 🔐

The encrypted release — brings vault encryption (finally!) plus UI improvements.

Vault encryption:

- Password-protected vaults using AES-256-GCM with Argon2id key derivation
- Automatic encryption of all new notes once a vault is secured
- File & folder name encryption (note content + folder names are encoded)
- One-click vault lock when stepping away
- Ability to encrypt an existing vault
- Warning when opening `.md` files inside a secured vault

UI / theme:

- Added 3 themes: Original, Modern, Agrume
- Responsive stats bar (stats / file name / save status adapt to window size)

## v3.6.0 (2025-02-25) 🔮

The reader release — the reader design was updated to be more in sync with the app overall.

- Literal links are auto-detected and mapped
- Improved design for checkboxes, tables, lists and more
- Code blocks can get a title, diff and line display; line numbers are removable per block
- Callout support, blockquotes rendered correctly
- Footnotes are autogenerated
- Zen mode (`ctrl + m`)
- Foldable sidebar (`ctrl + n`)
- Fixed file rename
- Scroll position is synced between reader and editor
- Available on the AUR

## v3.3.0 (2024-12-01) 🪩

The mirror release.

- Replaced the Markdown editor with CodeMirror, enabling Ctrl+Z and harmonizing the theme with the application
- Refactored the application user interface

## v3.2.4 (2024-11-21) 🙈

Manual release.

- Manually built installers to avoid a GitHub action config problem
- Basically the same version as v3.2.3

## v3.2.3 (2024-10-01) 👻

Improvement release.

- New search modal with `ctrl+k`
- New help modal with `ctrl+h`
- Information about the text change at the top of the editor
- Improved the UI and the code itself
- AUR is up to date

## v3.1.6 (2024-09-23) 🏴

The beta release via Wails app.

- First release of Tape, a very simple, not-bloated note-taking app
- With Tape, you can only take notes!

## v2.1.7 (2024-09-08) β

The beta release via Tauri.

- First release of **Tape**, a very simple, not-bloated note-taking app
- With Tape, you can only take notes!
- Next steps planned: polish the UI/UX and add a search bar to search across all notes
- Only Linux files provided at the time due to a Tauri build bug